          Concrete is one of the most widely used structural building materials in the world, composed of Portland cement, fine aggregate (sand), coarse aggregate (gravel or crushed stone), and clean water.
          Whether you are pouring a backyard patio slab, casting isolated deck footings, pouring round sonotube piers, building roadside curbs, or framing entrance stairs, calculating the exact volume of concrete is essential to budget properly and avoid cold joints caused by running out of material midway through a pour.
